<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12978"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Phoenix<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Phoenix<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->3-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, April 19, 2005 - 4:27 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Day 1, 4/19/2005 <BR> <BR>Local Media will have live coverage, starting as early as 7:30am.  For the media rules of engagement in State v. Rader see: <a href="http://www.sedgwickcounty.org/da/Dennis_Rader/pdf_files/Rader_Media_Guidelines.pdf" target=_top>http://www.sedgwickcounty.org/da/Dennis_Rader/pdf_ files/Rader_Media_Guidelines.pdf</a>  <BR> <BR>For the Kansas Supreme Court Rule and 18th Judicial District Court Rule see: <a href="http://www.newsconnect.com/cic/local.pdf" target=_top>http://www.newsconnect.com/cic/local.pdf</a>. <BR> <BR>Cox Cable channel 22 is carrying live, commercial-free, gavel to gavel coverage. <BR> <BR>I&#39;ll be in the courthouse at 9:00 am on another case. <BR> <BR>Should be interesting. <BR>  <BR>Phoenix<!--/Text--></td></tr>
